Round-11 audit, failure (3): "the N8 instruction was a per-residue
DEFAULT; the delivered patch made it opt-in with per_atom as the
default." v1 (delivered on evidence/round9-r2-2026-10-20 under
outputs/patches-n8-per-residue-altlocs/) is REJECTED on that point and
is preserved there byte-identical as the historical record; nothing on
the prior delivery is rewritten.

This series corrects the default exactly as directed:

- backend/tos/ingestion/processor.py — ALTLOC_POLICY flips from
  ALTLOC_POLICY_PER_ATOM to ALTLOC_POLICY_PER_RESIDUE. The selection
  logic itself is UNCHANGED from v1 (same two policies, same selector,
  same guarantees: exactly one atom per (chain, residue, atom_name)).
  per_atom remains available as an explicit opt-in
  (altloc_policy=ALTLOC_POLICY_PER_ATOM) carrying the original P0
  item 6 semantics byte-for-byte, so pre-N8 deliveries stay comparable.
  Comments and the IngestionProcessor.run docstring now state the v2
  default and record that the flip is an audit-directed semantic
  change, not a silent one.
- backend/tests/test_altloc_per_residue.py — updated for the new
  default: test_module_default_is_per_residue (was ..._is_per_atom),
  test_default_run_matches_explicit_per_residue (was ..._per_atom),
  test_default_is_chimera_safe_on_chimera_input (NEW: under the v2
  default the chimera fixture cannot mix conformers), renamed
  test_per_atom_optin_produces_mixed_conformers (documents the explicit
  opt-in path), test_cif_default_matches_per_residue +
  test_cif_per_atom_optin_matches_legacy (was test_cif_default_unchanged),
  and test_3erd_default_per_residue_asp321_still_conformer_a (was
  test_3erd_default_unchanged_by_patch; 3ERD ASP A 321 is a 0.50/0.50
  tie, per-residue totals tie, first-seen ID = A wins, so the pinned
  P0-era coordinate assertion still holds).

